{
  "name": "barracuda",
  "_about": "SCULPTED (2026-11-21, tools/creaturegen/rework/fish/barracuda.py): a great barracuda, 1.3 m -- a long round torpedo (its depth a seventh of its length), the long pointed head with a jutting UNDERBITE (the lower jaw well past the upper, its tip a knob) and the gape full of long uneven FANGS (`horn`s, the biggest at the front of the lower jaw); two small dorsal fins set FAR APART (the first spiny, over the pelvics; the second far back, over the anal), small pectorals, a big forked tail; steel-grey above, bright silver flanks with ~13 dark OBLIQUE BARS on the upper side and inky black blotches scattered low on the rear flank. Each fin is one membrane sheet. A SWIMMER.",
  "kind": "parts",
